# Git — implement first, PR only on request

The user owns `main`. Never land work there. Never merge PRs.

## Default

Implement. Leave **uncommitted**. No `commit` / `push` / `gh pr create` until asked. “PR” means open one, not merge.

## Commit

Conventional Commits (English) and push immediately. No PR unless asked. If a PR is already open, edit the title and body for **every** commit on the branch.

## PR

1. Branch off `main` (`feat/…` / `fix/…` / `docs/…`). Not on `main`. One concern per PR.
2. Commit, push, open a PR whose body covers all commits.
3. There is no CI yet. Do not invent jobs. If a check exists and fails, read the failing hunk and fix it. Do not watch a green run.
4. Stop. Give the PR URL.

Later commits: push and refresh the PR body.

## `main` updates

Fetch and **merge** `origin/main` into the PR head, then push. No rebase, no force. Conflicts: stop and say so. Do not fast-forward local `main` unless asked.

## Never

Unprompted commit, push, or PR (except merging `origin/main` into an open PR head). No push to `main`. No `gh pr merge`. No force-push to `main`.

## After they merge

Do not recreate the deleted head. `git fetch --prune` and delete the local branch if it remains.
